**************************************************************
                LCD-Demo
**************************************************************
We just completed a small demo showing Triplex LCD drive with
COP800 devices.
The documentation is finished and we have some PCB's available.
A demo can be reveived upon special request (via Mktg).
Please note, that the's approach of realizing a Triplex LCD drive
will not yield an optimal contrast.
The experiences in the past showed, that there is only little
tendency to return demos to FFB.
So please, do only request a demo if you see a serious chance to
place a design win and return a demo back to us if you or your
customer does not need it anymore.
Providing demos is very time consuming and costy.
Please return also other demos as far as no more needed.
**************************************************************


**************************************************************
         Datasheet COP820CJ
**************************************************************
There is a mistake in COP820CJ preliminary datasheet as of
Nov.1991 on page 19, second paragraph from the bottom (left side)
it says "IEDG selects the external interrupt edge(1=rising edge,
0=falling edge)".
******This is wrong !!*********
It should read ....(0=rising edge,1=falling edge)!
**************************************************************


**************************************************************
        COP820CJ-Hybrid
**************************************************************
The highest address of the internal EPROM (1FFF) must be programmed
with the followind data byte:
                   20 Pin DIP         28 Pin DIP/SO

Address 1FFF:         E7                   6F
***************************************************************


***************************************************************
                Duplicator-Board
***************************************************************
To program COP8780/COP-Hybrids with the Duplicator-Board
use the following configurations.

- Duplicator-Board, Firmsoftware 7451-006A(EPROM 27C64
  EPROM-Checksum 6060)

- COP800 programming scramblers for Hybrids(20/40DIL,28SO
  or 44/28PLCC)

- COP8780 programming scrambler for COP87XX(20/28/40DIL,28SO)

To update the Hybrid Duplicator-Board to COP8780/Hybrid-D.Board
replace the Firmsoftware to the latest version and use for
programming the COP87XX the new COP8780 programming scrambler.
***************************************************************


***************************************************************
                 Metalink-Probecard-Jumpers
***************************************************************
Jumpers W1-W4 are available on the probecards without
Brow Out indicator!
All jumper are available on the probecards with yellow LED
( VCC-Status/Brown out)
***************************************************************
                    W1-Jumper
***************************************************************
Probecard 880 (820,840,880,820CJ)
W1 Select RAM:
This Jumper determines how much RAM is available.
placed between the center post and the A post: 64 Bytes
placed between the center post and the B post: 128 Bytes

Probecard 888XX
W1 Select Halt mode:
This Jumper select the Halt Options.
placed between the center post and the A post: Halt disable
placed between the center post and the B post: Halt enable
***************************************************************
                    W2-Jumper
***************************************************************
All Probecards
W2 VCC Jumper, only available on the 2.3-6.0/2.5-6.0 Probecard
This jumper select the Probecard power supply.

placed between the center post and the PC post:
supplied from probecard VCC = 5 Volt

placed between the center post and the TAR post:
supplied from Target system via VCC/GND Pin of microcontroller
socket

On 4.5-5.5 probe cards this jumper is hardwired to the PC setting.
This must not be changend. Operating outside this voltage range
may permanently damage the probe card!
***************************************************************
                    W3/W4-Jumper
***************************************************************
All probecards
These jumpers select the clock source:

placed between the center post and the PC post: internal 10MHz
crystal clock is connected to the oscillator circuit

placed between the center post and the TAR post: either a target
crystal or clock driver can be used

***************************************************************
                   W6-Jumper
***************************************************************
Probecard 820CJ
This jumper select the Brown Out option:

placed between the center post and the A post: Brown Out disable
placed between the center post and the B post: Brown Out enable

All Probecards with LED:
The Brown Out indicator (yellow LED) will always light when a voltage
lower than the Brown Out voltage is detected, regardless of the state
of the jumper W6
Brown Out voltage for the 820CJ probecard is 2.34 Volt
Brown Out voltage for all other probecards is 2.52 Volt

**************************************************************
                        W7-Jumper
**************************************************************
All Probecards with LED:
The jumper W7 select the G7 options:

placed between the center post and the A post: G7 is available as
a general purpose input (RC-oscillator)

placed between the center post and the B post: CKO pin is emulated

When running with a target crystal W7 must be placed in the CKO (B)
position.
**************************************************************


**************************************************************
                   Metalink-bugs
**************************************************************

 Metalink-Software version 3.1 REV3, Model 3.029


1) B-pointer,Stackpointer,X-pointer and address 0FF(S-Register
   for 888CG/EG) are incorrectly cleared at reset. Those register
   are set to 00 by the Metalink Software upon reset, whereas in
   the real COP those register remain UNCHANGED upon reset.

2) Ram addresses 0B0-0BF (Timer 3 register, UART, etc.) can not
   be changed in the register window (COP888EG\CG).
   However changing them with Display RAM modify window works

